# Security & Data Sovereignty Guidelines

## Rules
- Never commit hardcoded secrets, Bearer tokens, or API credentials to version control.
- Ensure all outbound HTTP client requests validate destination hostnames against private IP ranges (RFC 1918, RFC 3927, 127.0.0.1/8, ::1) to eliminate SSRF vulnerabilities.
- Strip all personally identifiable information (PII) from error traces and telemetry payloads.
- All code must execute safely and locally without unvetted background network telemetry.